# R Style Rules

## Assignment and Pipe
- Assignment: `<-` always. Never `=` for assignment (only for function arguments).
- Pipe: `|>` (native pipe, R 4.1+). Never `%>%` (magrittr) in new code.
- One pipe step per line. Align pipes vertically.

## Naming
- Objects and functions: `snake_case`
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`
- Files: `snake_case.R`
- Quarto chunks: named, snake_case (`{r compute-features}`)

## Line Length and Spacing
- Max line length: 80 characters (lintr default)
- One blank line between function definitions
- Space after commas, around `<-`, around `|>` on its own line
- No trailing whitespace

## ggplot2 Standards
Every plot in a deliverable document must have:
```r
ggplot(data, aes(x = col_a, y = col_b)) +
  geom_point() +
  labs(
    title = "Descriptive title",
    x = "X-axis label (units)",
    y = "Y-axis label (units)",
    caption = "Source: {data source} | Analysis: {author}"
  ) +
  theme_minimal()
```
No default grey background in deliverables. `theme_grey()` only in exploratory chunks.

## Roxygen2 for Functions in R/
Every exported function gets roxygen2 docs:
```r
#' Compute churn risk features
#'
#' @param df A data frame with columns: tenure_days, monthly_spend
#' @return A data frame with added columns: tenure_months, high_value
#' @export
compute_features <- function(df) { ... }
```
